  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 37482923).\n\n## What changed\n- `vise::SelfCentering` gains `grip_depth` / `grip_width` (mm, 0 = off): a grip jaw, a step cut into each jaw's inside top edge. The jaw profile walks down the face to the ledge, in along it, down to the floor; the frame's z = 0 is the ledge (the floor the part sits on), so the vise body drops by `jaw_height - grip_depth`. Fit and an in-place `SetVise` edit both keep the stock seated on the ledge; the fixture/collision laws, stock simulation and the post gate read the stepped mesh.\n- Law (`check_grip`, refused by name at command creation): both figures or neither; finite, non-negative; depth < jaw height; width < jaw thickness; opening > 2 x width (ledges would meet under the stock); dovetail lip and grip step not both (\"a dovetail or a grip jaw, not both\").\n- `ViseParams::seat_height()` / `SelfCentering::seat()`.\n- Project: two optional keys on the `self_centering` object, written only when non-zero; older files read as no step and a stepless vise writes byte for byte as before. No project version move.\n- Dialog: \"Grip step depth\" / \"Grip step width\" rows with tooltips (dovetail rows get one too); the fit line says the stock sits on the grip steps and how far above the vise floor.\n- MCP: `add_builtin_vise` / `set_vise` `dimensions` take `grip_depth` / `grip_width`; the vise view reports them.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1274-grip-jaw.md`.\n\n## Tests\n- `crates/app/tests/self_centering_grip_jaw.rs` (new): `the_grip_jaw_carries_the_step_and_its_seat_is_the_frame_origin` (volume, bounds, steel/air at ledge and jaw), `bad_grip_figures_are_refused_by_name`, `a_grip_vise_seats_the_stock_on_the_ledge` (vise sits 12 mm lower than bed-seated for a 3 mm step on a 15 mm jaw), `the_fixture_law_judges_the_stepped_jaw` (face pass at z 9.5 struck by bed-seated jaws, clear on the grip step; pass at z 1 into the step blocks the post), `an_older_vise_key_reads_and_writes_unchanged_and_a_grip_round_trips` (old key byte for byte; save/reload; undo/redo).\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_self_centering_vise.rs`: grip dims through `set_vise`, refusals named, undo count.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/fixture_self_centering_tests.rs`: grip rows present for self-centering only; `a_grip_jaw_seats_the_stock_on_its_steps_and_places_in_one_step` (structural; no snapshot PNGs).\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`) and clippy `-D warnings` on app/ui on the final head f0e63454: green (app suites 18 s, ui suites 83 s; 0 failed); clippy clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Posed (tilted) grip vises in the 5-axis fixture laws beyond the shared mesh path; setup sheet (it does not state jaw forms).\n- An older build re-editing a grip vise would drop the step (it keeps the saved facets until edited) - noted in the decision file.\n\nChangelog: Self-centering vises get an optional grip jaw - a step (depth, width) on each jaw's inside top edge that the stock sits on; the fixture checks judge the stepped jaw (#1274)\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1274\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
